      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The results strongly suggest an issue beyond just the local physical layer, as the spike in latency appears progressively as the packets traverse the network hops. The significant and inconsistent jump in latency between hop 1 and hop 2, followed by the high packet loss, points toward congestion or instability somewhere along the path. It's more likely a network congestion issue on hop 2 or 3 rather than a simple routing table error.",
