      "content": "Random, cyclical spikes are a classic symptom of buffer exhaustion or resource contention on the older hardware of hop 2. Older routers often struggle with bursty traffic, leading to intermittent micro-outages as buffers overflow and packets are dropped. While hardware degradation is possible, the irregular nature strongly suggests that the router is being overloaded by bursts of traffic that exceed its current processing or buffering capacity.",
